    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0226" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg138"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tsui to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1891</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 27.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a paper which
                    has been received at this legation signed by a number of citizens of the United
                    States residing on Whidbey Island, in the State of Washington, representing that
                    injustice is being done to the Chinese subjects in that locality at the hands of
                    officials of the United States Treasury Department and the United States
                    commissioner of that district.</p>
                <p>This legation has no disposition to encourage any violation of the laws of the
                    United States on the part of Chinese subjects, but it feels that it can rely
                    upon the Federal Government of the United States to see that justice is extended
                    to the Chinese residents who are lawfully in this country, and that the Treasury
                    Department will be pleased to direct its officials in the locality mentioned in
                    the accompanying paper not to violate the universally acknowledged principle of
                    law and evidence that persons accused of crime must be proven guilty, and that
                    said officials should not harass peaceable persons by illegal arrests.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsui Kwo Yin.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d102-a1.xml" xpointer="d102-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
